Find LCM of their times\begin{align*}
\text{asin(}\frac{\pi 6^2}{30})&=\frac{6\pi}{5}\text{                      \hfill \text{asin(}\frac{\pi 8^2}{40})&=\frac{8\pi}{5}    \hfill \text{asin(}\frac{\pi 10^2}{50})&=\pi 
\end{align*}So the LCM is 8\pi so they finish coatinh three workers at the same time at 8\pi minutes.
Then do 8pi divided numbers.\begin{align*}
\frac{8\pi}{6}&=\frac{4\pi}{3}\text{worked on 4th donut}\\
\frac{8\pi}{8}&=\pi\text{worked on 1st donut}\\
\frac{8\pi}{10}&=\frac{4\pi}{5}\text{worked on 5th donut}
\end{align*}<answer>4th  </answer>

